&lt;p&gt;This dataset contains the complete replication artifacts for the paper &lt;em&gt;Identifiability of Relational Queries in Multi-View Pretraining&lt;/em&gt; (Ratan Bahadur Thapa and Daniel Hern&amp;aacute;ndez). The paper studies when a relational query is &lt;em&gt;identifiable&lt;/em&gt; from a data-integration interface&amp;mdash;that is, when every legal completion of the data consistent with the interface returns the same answer&amp;mdash;and introduces two polynomial-time schema-design algorithms: CheckCert, which decides certification via an attribute-closure certificate, and Greedy-MinAug, which selects a near-minimum set of interface actions (resolvers, crosswalks, shared identifiers) that make a query identifiable.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The deposit has three parts:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experiment code (Python).&lt;/strong&gt; Implementations of both algorithms, the full experimental pipeline (error-floor, capability-jump, minimum-augmentation, certificate-benchmark, scalability, and real-world witness-discovery experiments), and the builders for every dataset used in the paper&amp;mdash;a synthetic benchmark with exhaustive ground truth, the BibInteg bibliographic dataset, and the real cross-source datasets CrossKG-DBLP (OpenAlex &amp;times; DBLP), Amazon-Google, and Fodors-Zagat, alongside the WDC schema case study. All figures and tables are regenerable from a documented set of &lt;code&gt;Makefile&lt;/code&gt; targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lean&amp;nbsp;4 formalization.&lt;/strong&gt; Machine-checked proofs of the paper's core results: correctness of the atom-wise closure certificate, the information-theoretic 1/2 error floor, the robust-threshold guarantee, the FD/Armstrong closure correspondence, and the reduction of identifiability to query determinacy over overlap-projection views (including Fano's inequality). The distributional Fano corollary, the general capability-jump theorem, and the MinAug greedy bound and NP-hardness are documented as open in the formalization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplementary material.&lt;/strong&gt; Artifacts referenced by the paper: BibInteg statistics, extended ML results, and FD-completeness curves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Software dependencies and exact reproduction commands are given in the included &lt;code&gt;&lt;a href="https://darus.uni-stuttgart.de/file.xhtml?fileId=622472"&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/code&gt;; provenance and licensing are in &lt;code&gt;CITATION.cff&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;LICENSE&lt;/code&gt;. The artifacts accompany the arXiv preprint &lt;a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.04735"&gt;arXiv:2607.04735&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt; Use persistent identifiers from Software Heritage (

) to cite individual files or even lines of the source code.
